Followed, not copied, in crates/kgraf-orchestrator/src/orchestrator.rs.
The ROADMAP Phase 4 build plan names `agents/subagent_execution_tool/`; at
this commit that directory holds only `notification_events.rs`, and the
delegate lifecycle lives in `subagent_handler.rs`. What transfers: a delegate
runs with its own cancellation, its events are forwarded to the parent while
it runs (`notification_tx`), and its result is collected when its stream
ends. kGraf's worker runtime already provides spawn, handle, cancel and
the event stream, so no goose code is copied. Deliberately different: goose
logs and ignores an extension that fails to load for a subagent (`debug!`);
kGraf checks readiness, tool discovery included, before a worker gets
capacity, and refuses the dispatch (SR-008).
